    "result_text": "The build passes and all tests are green. There's a single acceptance test class (`AcceptanceTest`), which verifies the full behavior.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day roll in `OwnerRestControllerV1.rollToBusinessDay` to skip public holidays as well as weekends.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant with the fixed list: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Replaced the old weekend-only `switch` (which just jumped Sat\u2192Mon / Sun\u2192Mon) with a loop that advances the date one day at a time while it lands on a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday. This correctly handles the chained case where rolling off a weekend lands on a holiday, or a holiday falls adjacent to a weekend (e.g. `2026-12-25` and `2026-12-28` bracketing a weekend).\n- Extracted a small `isWeekend` helper for readability and updated the Javadoc.\n\nThe loop mirrors the `toBusinessDay` reference algorithm the acceptance test suite uses (weekend + holiday set, advance one day), so the stored `registrationDate` and everything derived from it always falls on a non-holiday business day. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
