    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change extends the existing `rollToBusinessDay` helper in place rather than introducing a parallel mechanism, which keeps the business-day logic in the single unit that already owned it. Specifics that make it clean:\n\n- The weekend-or-holiday roll is unified into one `while` loop advancing a day at a time, so the two skip conditions share one code path instead of being duplicated or special-cased.\n- Extracting `isWeekend` gives the loop a readable predicate and keeps the `switch` responsibility (weekday classification) separate from the roll-forward concern \u2014 a natural, minimal decomposition.\n- `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` is a `private static final Set.of(...)` placed adjacent to the method that uses it, with a Javadoc explaining its role; membership testing via `contains` is the idiomatic fit.\n- The Javadoc on `rollToBusinessDay` was updated to match the new behavior rather than left stale.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all growth, and the additions sit consistently alongside the pre-existing helper.",
    "review_cost_usd": 0.0988,
